From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:26:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add JSON-Lines activity logger for Hybrid AI Core decisions

Per docs/designs/hybrid-ai-core-activity-logger.md:

- dlls/game.h/.cpp: two new CVars, ai_hybrid_log (master switch,
  default 0) and ai_hybrid_log_file (output path, default
  ai_hybrid_log.jsonl), independent of ai_hybrid/ai_hybrid_debug.
- dlls/ai_hybrid.h/.cpp: AIHybrid_MaybeLogActivity() appends one
  JSON-Lines record per DecideAction() call (time, entity, action,
  previous action, score, confidence, context, whether hybrid AI is
  enabled). Keeps a lazily-opened FILE* alive for the process
  lifetime (unlike stats.cpp's open/write/close-per-call pattern,
  since decisions happen far more often) and fflushes after every
  write so a crash doesn't lose the tail. Hand-rolled JSON is safe
  here since every field is a number/bool/controlled enum-name
  string, never arbitrary text. ai_hybrid_core.h/.cpp untouched -
  logging is engine-adapter-only, same layering as every other phase.
- dlls/hgrunt.cpp: captures DecideAction()'s previously-discarded
  return value and passes it to the new logger, from the same
  throttled block that already calls AIHybrid_MaybeLogDebug().

Verified: core tests unaffected (still pass), client.so/vgui.so
byte-identical to the pre-Phase-A baseline (only hl.so differs), and
the exact printf format round-trips through a JSON parser. Manual
in-game verification of the generated log file is still open.

